scoswm (0.5.7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Rework the right desktop rule as a buffered six-pixel surface stacked
    above ordinary application frames, with an empty X SHAPE input region so
    its pixels cannot intercept Close buttons or application content. Retain
    wallpaper fallback columns and leave the overlay unmapped without SHAPE.
  * Center the Wi-Fi arcs above their dot, add a compact numeric month/day and
    year between power and clock, and keep Wi-Fi/power controls adjacent.
    Distinguish hosted hotspots from joined client networks, preserve
    simultaneous per-card connections and sort active network rows first.
  * Add a right-click Windows overview with MRU tiles, on-demand X11 captures,
    title/icon fallbacks, a large upper-left recent window, clean outer
    spacing, click/keyboard activation and safe stale-window handling.
  * Require Cancel-default confirmation for WM restart/exit, suspend, reboot
    and power off from both power and desktop menus; Lock remains immediate.
  * Add unit/graphical coverage for hotspot merging, active-first ordering,
    bar geometry, power cancellation, click-through rule input and real-client
    overview behavior; retain prior Files, Bash/PTY, shortcut, scrolling and
    crash regressions. Physical display/wireless behavior still needs target-
    system retesting.

