scoswm (0.5.6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Split shortcut activation into focus-or-launch and always-launch-new
    paths. Double-clicking a desktop or taskbar shortcut now starts another
    real application instance even when one is running; a single click
    activates the most recently active matching window without spawning.
  * Preserve no-motion drag/drop handling, delayed single-launch behavior for
    unopened taskbar pins, desktop selection and surface-independent context
    menus. Receive root button releases so fast desktop clicks cannot leave
    a shortcut stuck in its drag state.
  * Remove all reported normal-build format-truncation diagnostics in Wi-Fi
    status/adapter rows and standalone Files titles/status messages, plus
    optimization-dependent SysMon and interface-name sites, with bounded
    display formatting rather than warning suppression.
  * Add real-X11-client regressions for desktop/taskbar multi-instance
    launching and most-recent-window restore, while retaining all previous
    scrolling, Files, terminal, withdrawal/reuse and Wi-Fi checks.

