scoswm (0.5.5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Bundle the original-style scos-files X11/POSIX file manager and make it
    the default Files action, with real navigation, folder creation,
    non-overwriting rename, desktop opening, a KDE desktop entry and icons.
    Retain explicit external-manager overrides and their launch regressions.
  * Repaint only changed terminal rows during Bash/readline echo and arrow
    movement, preserve full Expose/resize fallbacks, and ellipsize long tab
    titles before the visible, clickable Close control.
  * Add a dedicated override-redirect right-rule surface instead of relying
    only on root wallpaper pixels, retaining the existing inset and fallback.
  * Add a lightweight taskbar Wi-Fi panel with native per-adapter status,
    simultaneous-connection rows, scrolling, nonblocking nmcli scan/connect,
    and explicit per-interface connection arguments. NetworkManager remains
    optional for Arch and Debian and no network daemon is added to SCosWM.
  * Add real-directory, multi-adapter parser, standalone Files UI, incremental
    terminal, long-title Close, dedicated-rule and delayed fake-nmcli tests;
    preserve all prior scrolling, crash, withdrawal and drag/drop checks.

