scoswm (0.5.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Bundle four dedicated SCos application icon sets (Terminal, Files,
    SysMon and Settings) at 16–256 px and use those names everywhere the
    built-ins appear, including desktop pins and the Windows picker.
  * Add a deterministic, dependency-free artwork generator and a complete
    SCos Xcursor theme with common cursor aliases. Select it explicitly in
    the session and publish matching X resources and GTK XSETTINGS from the
    WM, covering Qt/GTK application interiors without another daemon.
  * Make the right desktop rule two pixels wide so an inner column remains
    visible even if the physical display clips its final column.
  * Replace green-on-green selection states with bright accent backgrounds
    and dark text across the launcher, menus, Settings and taskbar hover /
    launch states. Highlight the active Settings text field consistently.
  * Retain the pins-only taskbar and client-preserving withdrawal behavior;
    expand graphical checks for all built-in images, cursor settings,
    high-contrast selections, both right-edge columns and 20 reuse cycles.

