scoswm (0.5.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Keep only permanent pinned shortcuts on the main taskbar. Running
    windows now appear exclusively in the Windows picker, with their real
    application icons and stable row targets; animations target the picker.
  * Preserve client windows across ordinary unmap/withdrawal by reparenting
    them to the root before destroying only the WM frame. This fixes the
    destructive rapid unmap/reuse path found in close/reopen stress testing.
  * Keep launcher application names readable on their highlighted rows and
    rotate the power symbol so its circular opening faces upward.
  * Keep taskbar menus and built-in Settings/SysMon panels open after the
    opening click's release. Add graphical coverage for picker-only operation,
    20 window-reuse cycles and live persisted 28/32 px taskbar scaling.

