scoswm (0.5.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Double-buffer taskbar, frame, launcher, menu, SysMon and Settings
    painting; reuse the desktop backing pixmap on expose and avoid
    erase-before-redraw flashes during terminal and frame resizing.
  * Keep ordinary application frames below the taskbar, make taskbar
    activation respond on a single press, scale and centre all bar
    controls, and add a contrasting close-button hover state.
  * Animate minimise/restore with a separate placeholder without resizing
    the real application; avoid duplicate client geometry requests when
    moving windows. Terminal resize keeps a complete backing image.
  * Inherit the session cursor in SCos Terminal, centre desktop labels,
    and draw explicit right/bottom desktop border lines.
  * Install dedicated SCos Terminal hicolor icons and a KDE window-class
    mapping; support SVG application icons through the optional desktop
    gdk-pixbuf/librsvg loader in addition to built-in PNG/XPM decoding.
  * Add repeatable headless graphical regressions for painting, layout,
    stacking, cursor inheritance, icons and resize-free animations.

