scoswm (0.5.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add scos-terminal, a standalone SCos-styled Xlib terminal with tabs,
    scrollback, UTF-8, colors, fullscreen application support, selection
    and clipboard integration. It runs a real interactive Bash on a PTY,
    not a simulated command parser.
  * Install a freedesktop application entry so SCos Terminal can be
    launched independently from KDE and other desktops.
  * Prefer scos-terminal for the WM's Terminal action while preserving
    explicitly configured terminal commands and external fallbacks.
  * Request system titlebars for Firefox and ordinary GTK applications
    in the SCosWM session, without overriding explicit environment
    settings; document Chromium's own system-titlebar preference.
  * Add terminal parser, resize/scrollback and real-Bash PTY tests.

